## What You Must Do

**All employees working with composite materials:**

1. **Verify Exhaust:** Visually confirm exhaust is operating (check airflow indicator) before any oven operation.

2. **Check Alarms:** Confirm alarm system status is "NORMAL" on the control panel. Report any "MAINTENANCE" or "BYPASS" status immediately.

3. **Stop Work:** If you observe any abnormal conditions, stop work and notify your supervisor immediately.

4. **Report:** Any unusual odors or respiratory discomfort must be reported immediately. Seek medical attention if symptoms persist.

## Respiratory Protection

Until redundant sensors are installed, the following PPE is required in the curing area:

| Area | Required PPE |
|------|--------------|
| Curing oven room | Half-face respirator with organic vapor cartridge |
| Adjacent areas | Optional (recommended during operations) |

## Manager Responsibilities

Supervisors and managers must:

1. Review this bulletin with all affected employees within 24 hours
2. Ensure pre-work checklists are completed properly
3. Physically verify exhaust operation before authorizing work
4. Never sign off on work permits without verification

